  "issue_number": 3,
  "issue_title": "Add local submission bundle validator for miners",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n`CONTRIBUTOIN.md` tells miners to ensure `submissions/final_model/` is complete before opening a PR, but the repo has no local tool that checks the bundle. Incomplete or malformed submissions (missing `best_theta.npy`, wrong theta length, broken `summary.json`) only fail later in the validator backend / PR automation queue.\r\n\r\n## Proposed feature\r\n\r\nAdd a zero-network CLI (e.g. `python scripts/validate_submission.py`) that miners run before packaging / opening a PR.\r\n\r\n## Checks\r\n\r\n- Required files present: `best_theta.npy`, `summary.json`\r\n- Optional files reported if present: `history.json`, `eval.json`\r\n- `best_theta.npy` loads as a float vector with length matching the coordinator `ParamSpec.n_total` (13312 by default)\r\n- `summary.json` is valid JSON and includes useful keys (`benchmark`, `n_total`, `best_fitness`, `pool`) when available; warn if `n_total` disagrees with the theta length\r\n- Exit non-zero with clear errors on failure; print a short OK summary on success\r\n\r\n## Why useful\r\n\r\n- Catches submission mistakes before PR automation uploads the bundle\r\n- Matches the contribution guide (make sure the model bundle is complete)\r\n- Offline / no API keys required, so cheap for every miner\r\n\r\n## Acceptance\r\n\r\n- Script + unit tests covering missing files, wrong shape, and a valid fixture\r\n- Brief docs note in `CONTRIBUTOIN.md` / README miner workflow\r\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-08T20:20:10.000Z",
  "test_cmd": [
    "python",
    "-m",
    "pytest",
    "--tb=short",
    "-q",
